  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>While you aren't wearing armor or wielding a Shield, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Dance Virtuoso.</strong> You have Advantage on any Charisma (Performance) check you make that involves you dancing.</p><p><strong>Unarmored Defense.</strong> Your base Armor Class equals 10 plus your Dexterity and Charisma modifiers.</p><p><strong>Agile Strikes.</strong> When you expend a use of your Bardic Inspiration as part of an action, a Bonus Action, or a Reaction, you can make one Unarmed Strike as part of that action, Bonus Action, or Reaction.</p><p><strong>Bardic Damage.</strong> You can use Dexterity instead of Strength for the attack rolls of your Unarmed Strikes. When you deal damage with an Unarmed Strike, you can deal Bludgeoning damage equal to a roll of your Bardic Inspiration die plus your Dexterity modifier, instead of the strike's normal damage. This roll doesn't expend the die.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-edFgTVLwqcuabKeK\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>This feature includes an Active Effect that sets up your Unarmored Defense which can be disabled if you would prefer to use armor.</p><p>The <strong>Unarmed Strike</strong> activity uses Dexterity and a Bardic Inspiration die for damage.</p><p>You are also granted an <strong>Unarmed Strike</strong> item which includes the changes.</p></section>",
